@startuml mcp_state
!include style.iuml
title MCP integration, states

hide empty description

[*] --> disabled : created

state disabled : never probed
state active
state unreachable <<accent>>

disabled --> active : PUT /v1/mcp/{id}
active --> disabled : PUT /v1/mcp/{id}
unreachable --> disabled : PUT /v1/mcp/{id}

active --> unreachable : probe failed
unreachable --> active : probe ok

note right of disabled
  The probe skips this state,
  so nothing leaves it but an operator.
end note
@enduml
